Media / MediaDB — licensing
===========================

This repository contains two different things under two different regimes, and the data half
is NOT under a single licence. Read the schedule.

  CODE   -> MIT (below)
  DATA   -> per upstream source. There is no blanket data licence.

Machine-readable schedule:  tools/licenses.tsv
Attribution notices:        NOTICE
Per-record licence:         each medium's provenance block carries `license`, `license_url`,
                            `license_source`, `commercial_use` and `commercial_use_ok`.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHY THIS FILE CHANGED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Until this revision, this file placed "everything under data/, and the media records" under
CC-BY-4.0. That was wrong, and wrong in the direction that transfers risk to the reader:
CC BY 4.0 s.2(a)(1) grants use "for any purpose, even commercially", and 1,189 of the 13,515
media (8.8%) come from upstream sources that grant no such right. Measured by the
quantitative content that gives the resource its value rather than by record count, the
exposure is larger: 10,737 of 14,341 non-null concentration values (74.9%) come from sources
that are non-commercial or carry no grant at all.

Nothing has been removed to fix this. Every record stays; each is labelled with the terms it
actually carries, and a reader who needs a commercially usable subset can select it.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DATA — LICENCE SCHEDULE BY SOURCE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Record counts are of 13,515 media, resolved from each record's own provenance evidence (URL
host, DOI, citation text) by tools/stages/source_identity.py — never from its filename.

COMMERCIALLY REDISTRIBUTABLE  (12,326 media, 91.2%)

  USDA FoodData Central .................. 7,424 media
      CC0 1.0 Universal (public domain dedication)
      https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
      "USDA FoodData Central data are in the public domain and they are not copyrighted.
       They are published under CC0 1.0 Universal (CC0 1.0)."  — fdc.nal.usda.gov/api-guide,
      retrieved 2026-09-06. Attribution requested, not required.

  DSMZ MediaDive ......................... 3,148 media
      CC BY 4.0 — https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
      "MediaDive (c) 2022 by DSMZ is licensed under CC BY 4.0" — mediadive.dsmz.de/imprint,
      retrieved 2026-09-06. Attribution AND indication of the licence are required
      (CC BY 4.0 s.3(a)(1)(C)); this repository did not indicate the licence before this
      schedule existed. Of these, 1,143 are JCM (RIKEN) media and 105 are CCAP media that
      MediaDive aggregates; see NOTICE.

  Primary literature via GrowthDB ........ 1,369 media
  Classic / standard formulations ........   297 media
  Primary literature (GEM papers) ........    88 media
      CC BY 4.0, asserted by this project over ITS OWN compilation, mapping and encoding.
      The formulations themselves are facts stated in the cited publications; the
      publications are not redistributed here. Users must still cite the primary work
      recorded in each record's provenance.citation.

NOT COMMERCIALLY REDISTRIBUTABLE  (1,189 media, 8.8%) — kept, labelled, and filterable

  FooDB .................................... 701 media
      CC BY-NC 4.0 — https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/
      "Use and re-distribution of the data, in whole or in part, for commercial purposes
       requires explicit permission of the authors and explicit acknowledgment of the source
       material (FooDB)" — foodb.ca/about, retrieved 2026-09-06 (first-party).

  MediaDB (Institute for Systems Biology) .. 471 media
      NO LICENCE GRANTED. "(c) 2014, Institute for Systems Biology, All Rights Reserved"
      — mediadb.systemsbiology.net/defined_media/, retrieved 2026-09-06 (first-party).
      Redistribution permission has not been obtained. This is the single largest contributor
      of quantitative data in the resource (8,397 of 14,341 concentration values, 58.6%).
      Contact: mediadb@systemsbiology.org.

  Human Metabolome Database (HMDB 5.0) ....... 9 media
      CC BY-NC 4.0. "All data and metadata in the HMDB are released under the Creative
      Commons (CC) Attribution-NonCommercial (NC) 4.0 International Licensing condition."
      hmdb.ca is Cloudflare-gated and returns HTTP 403 to every retrieval method tried on
      2026-09-06, so this quote is from the first-party page as captured by the Internet
      Archive on 2026-01-02:
      https://web.archive.org/web/20260102200014/https://hmdb.ca/about

  Bovine Metabolome Database (BMDB) .......... 5 media
      Custom terms, commercial use by explicit permission. The BMDB about page states no
      Creative Commons licence at all — only the permission clause — so these records are
      NOT labelled CC BY-NC. bovinedb.ca/about, retrieved 2026-09-06 (first-party).

  HMDB tables republished in an open-access paper ... 3 media
      Treated as CC BY-NC 4.0 (the upstream HMDB terms). Their immediate source is an
      open-access CC BY paper, but republication in a CC BY paper does not relicense the
      underlying HMDB values. Flagged license_review_required in the data pending resolution.

UNRESOLVED — 8 media carry `license_review_required: true`
      5 classic formulations (std_halobacterium, std_marine_broth_2216, std_methanobacterium,
      std_nitrobacter, std_nitrosomonas) whose provenance URL points at MediaDive, so their
      composition may have come from a CC BY source requiring attribution, plus the 3 records
      above. They are flagged rather than silently claimed.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT A USER MUST DO
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Cite the ORIGINAL SOURCE of every medium you use. It is in that medium's `provenance`.
2. For any commercial use, filter to `provenance.commercial_use_ok == true` (12,326 media),
   or obtain permission from the rights-holder named in tools/licenses.tsv.
3. When you redistribute MediaDive-derived records, indicate the CC BY 4.0 licence, not only
   the attribution — CC BY 4.0 s.3(a)(1)(C) requires it.
4. Read NOTICE. It carries the attributions this project owes upstream.

Nothing in this file is legal advice, and none of these labels is a warranty. Each row of
tools/licenses.tsv records where its terms were read from and on what date, so you can
re-verify any of them yourself.


